.TH BADAPPLESTEIN-BUILD 1 "July 2026" "BadAppleStein 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
badapplestein-build \- build a source library from PDFs and images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B badapplestein build
.RB [ options ]
.I sources_dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B badapplestein build
scans
.I sources_dir
for PDF files and image files (PNG, JPEG, TIFF, BMP), extracts multi\-resolution
feature descriptors from each page or image, and writes two binary files to the
library directory:
.B features.bin
and
.BR registry.bin .
.PP
These files are consumed by
.BR badapplestein\-encode (1)
during the arrange stage to match video frames against source pages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-library " " \fIdir\fR
Output library directory.
Default:
.BR ~/.badapplestein/library/ .
The directory is created if it does not exist.
.TP
.BR \-\-bits " " \fIn\fR
Bit depth for quantised feature descriptors.
Default: 8.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-edges
Skip Canny edge detection.
Edge features improve match accuracy but increase build time.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Include colour channel histograms in addition to greyscale features.
Increases memory usage and file size.
.TP
.BR \-\-scales " " \fIn\fR
Number of scale levels for the multi\-scale feature pyramid.
Default: 3.
.TP
.B \-\-multi\-scale
Alias for
.BR \-\-scales\ 3 .
Included for convenience.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIn\fR
Number of worker threads for PDF rendering and feature extraction.
Defaults to the number of available CPU cores.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print detailed progress to stderr, including per\-file extraction statistics.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress all non\-error output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON progress messages to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B features.bin
Binary blob containing quantised feature descriptors for every page.
Pages are stored sequentially; the offset for page
.I n
is computed from the page dimension metadata in
.BR registry.bin .
Each descriptor is a compact histogram (greyscale or colour) at each
scale level.
.TP
.B registry.bin
Fixed\-size header followed by an array of page records.
Each record contains:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Page index (within the source PDF or image).
.IP \(bu 2
Source filename.
.IP \(bu 2
Width and height in pixels.
.IP \(bu 2
Byte offset and length into
.BR features.bin .
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a library from a folder of source documents:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein build ~/my\-sources/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build with colour features and 5 scale levels:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein build \-\-color \-\-scales 5 ~/my\-sources/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build into a custom library path with verbose output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein build \-\-library /data/library \-\-verbose ~/my\-sources/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR badapplestein (1),
.BR badapplestein-encode (1)
.SH AUTHORS
BadAppleStein contributors.
